CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION fn_get_status(p_order_id NUMBER)
  RETURN VARCHAR2
IS
  l_status orders.status%TYPE;
BEGIN
  SELECT status INTO l_status
  FROM orders
  WHERE order_id = p_order_id;
  RETURN l_status;
EXCEPTION
  WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN RETURN 'NOT_FOUND';
  WHEN TOO_MANY_ROWS THEN RETURN 'AMBIGUOUS';
END fn_get_status;
/
The SELECT INTO raises NO_DATA_FOUND when no row matches, which the handler converts into a predictable 'NOT_FOUND' sentinel so callers avoid exception-handling boilerplate. TOO_MANY_ROWS is defensive here since order_id is a primary key and cannot actually return duplicates, but the handler documents intent. Returning sentinel strings trades strictness for caller convenience; if distinct handling is required, re-raise NO_DATA_FOUND instead and let the caller catch it. Note the EXCEPTION section must appear after the executable body in the same block scope.

