CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION fn_table_count(p_table VARCHAR2)
  RETURN NUMBER
IS
  l_cnt NUMBER;
BEGIN
  EXECUTE IMMEDIATE 'SELECT COUNT(*) FROM ' || p_table INTO l_cnt;
  RETURN l_cnt;
END fn_table_count;
/

SELECT fn_table_count('EVENTS') AS event_rows FROM dual;
EXECUTE IMMEDIATE compiles and runs the concatenated statement at runtime, with the INTO clause capturing the result into the local variable. This is the standard dynamic-SQL shape for operations where the table name cannot be hardcoded. Because the identifier is interpolated, this function is injection-prone if p_table ever comes from user input; harden it with DBMS_ASSERT.SQL_OBJECT_NAME to validate the name, or restrict callers to trusted code paths.

