CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION fn_business_days(p_start DATE, p_end DATE)
  RETURN NUMBER
IS
  l_cnt NUMBER := 0;
  l_dt  DATE := TRUNC(p_start);
BEGIN
  WHILE l_dt <= TRUNC(p_end) LOOP
    IF TO_CHAR(l_dt, 'DY', 'NLS_DATE_LANGUAGE=ENGLISH') NOT IN ('SAT', 'SUN')
       AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT NULL FROM holidays WHERE holiday_dt = l_dt)
    THEN
      l_cnt := l_cnt + 1;
    END IF;
    l_dt := l_dt + 1;
  END LOOP;
  RETURN l_cnt;
END fn_business_days;
/

The loop walks each calendar day in the inclusive range, counting only weekdays not present in the holidays table. The explicit NLS_DATE_LANGUAGE=ENGLISH is essential: TO_CHAR with 'DY' returns localized abbreviations, so on a French or Spanish session 'SAT' would never match and weekends would be silently counted. This day-by-day approach is simple and correct for short spans; for year-length ranges prefer a set-based calendar join for better performance.

